{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CgYtHW5q3Fh4FbQXZ1iJk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"name\": \"MotionBricks (NVIDIA)\", \"url\": \"https://github.com/NVlabs/motionbricks\"},\n    {\"name\": \"MotionBricks paper\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.24833\"},\n    {\"name\": \"motionbricks-blender (add-on)\", \"url\": \"https://github.com/hyun2xyz/motionbricks-blender\"},\n    {\"name\": \"motionbricks-blender release v0.1.0\", \"url\": \"https://github.com/hyun2xyz/motionbricks-blender/releases/tag/v0.1.0\"},\n    {\"name\": \"Codex\", \"url\": null},\n    {\"name\": \"Claude Code\", \"url\": null}\n  ],\n  \"on_screen_text\": \"NVlabs/motionbricks | Code Issues 9 Pull requests 2 Actions Projects Security Insights | motionbricks Public | Notifications Fork 42 | About | Official implementation of MotionBricks: Scalable Real-Time Motions with Modular Latent & Generative Model and Smart Primitives (SIGGRAPH 2026) | Readme License Contributing | MOTIONBRICKS | 1 token = 4 poses | README Contributing License Security | Citation | If you use this code in your research, please cite: | @article{yang2026motionbricks, title = {MotionBricks: Scalable Real-Time Motions with Modular Latent & Generative Model and Smart Primitives}, author = {...}, journal = {ACM Transactions on Graphics (TOG)}, year = {2026}, volume = {45}, number = {4}, doi = {10.1145/3011334}} | License | Code, documentation, models, and sample motions have different licenses: | README Contributing License Security | Documentation and media: NVIDIA-authored documentation text and media (images, screenshots, and videos, including the files in docs/media/) use Creative Commons Attribution (CC BY 4.0) | Models: NVIDIA Open Model Agreement. This covers the SOMA and G1 checkpoints on Hugging Face and the ONNX models. It permits commercial use and redistribution of modified models, subject to the agreement's terms. Licensed by NVIDIA Corporation under the NVIDIA Open Model Agreement. | Sample motions: NVIDIA Sample Data License. The covered human BVH and retargeted G1 CSV clips are for evaluating and testing NVIDIA technologies. The sample-data notice lists the covered files and credits Bones. These sample terms are separate from the model terms. | Licenses for dependencies and bundled robot assets are in licenses. Exporter dependency licenses are in tools/crmo/licenses. | This project downloads and installs additional components under their own license terms. Review those terms before use. | First steps | PS C:\\\\tutorial> Expand-Archive motionbricks-blender-main.zip -DestinationPath . | PS C:\\\\tutorial> dir .\\\\motionbricks-blender-main\\\\sources | Mode LastWriteTime Length Name | PS C:\\\\tutorial> cd motionbricks-blender-main\\\\sources | PS C:\\\\tutorial> python .\\\\motionbricks-blender.py | Code open source Apache 2.0 | hyun2xyz/motionbricks-blender | Code Issues Pull requests Actions Projects Security Insights | motionbricks-blender Public | Notifications Fork 0 | About | Free, unofficial Blender add-on: import NVIDIA MotionBricks motion as an animated character, plus a Scene Preview recorder | animation blender motion-editor motion-generation | Readme License | hyun2xyz/motionbricks-blender | main | motionbricks-blender / AGENTS.md | hyun2xyz and claude AGENTS.md: outline and track check on Windows | Preview Code Blame | Instructions for AI coding agents (Codex, Claude Code, and others) | @index.opensource | @hyun2xyz\",\n  \"key_claims\": [\n    \"The character started from zero motion data, just a T-pose, with no motion clips used as input.\",\n    \"MotionBricks is NVIDIA's real-time motion model, presented at SIGGRAPH 2026.\",\n    \"The model connects the character's current pose to a target pose placed ahead, generating every in-between frame in about 3 milliseconds.\",\n    \"MotionBricks' code is open source (Apache 2.0); the model itself is not open source but can be used, including commercially, under the NVIDIA Open Model Agreement.\",\n    \"NVIDIA's sample motions are for evaluation only and were not used as inputs in this experiment.\",\n    \"On a zigzag course, a new target pose (shown in blue) is continually placed just ahead of the character as it moves, driving continuous walking.\",\n    \"A free, unofficial Blender add-on (GPL-3.0-or-later) was built to import the generated walk as an animated character.\",\n    \"The tested workflow requires an NVIDIA RTX GPU, Windows or Linux, Blender 4.2+, and about 12 GB of disk space.\",\n    \"Links to the add-on, project/demo, MotionBricks code, and paper are provided, and the link can be given directly to a coding agent like Codex or Claude Code to use the project.\",\n    \"README images used are © NVIDIA under CC BY 4.0 (cropped); this project is unofficial and not affiliated with NVIDIA.\"\n  ],\n  \"info_channel\": \"caption\"\n}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9193,"cache_read_input_tokens":3289,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9193},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d6277619-56b6-4a97-9e75-d9f4cc1e2648","uuid":"5fce83db-1e7f-4407-95cf-8652cd83700c","timestamp":"2026-10-30T18:21:40.892Z","request_id":"req_011CgYtHVmy1FFoA8G1BqUa6"}
